<onlyinclude>'''Autopoiesis''' is a theory of living organization developed by Humberto Maturana and Francisco Varela. It describes a system whose network of processes produces and maintains the components and boundary that make that same network possible.

== Explanation ==
A living cell makes many of its own molecular components and maintains a membrane that helps organize those processes. It still exchanges matter and energy with the environment. Autopoiesis emphasizes self-production, not independence from external resources, and differs from reproduction of new organisms.

